% Exposure of horns (tasks.org, aida-rational-closure; the E2 probe of
% 2026-10-14): a lemma proved inside an argument is a node of its own.
%
%   argP  : P from the axiom qp : Q->P and a presumption of Q
%   argQ  : Q from pq : P->Q and its own lemma for P, proved from
%           rp : R->P and a presumption of R
%   killR : refutes R strictly, from nR : ~R
%
% argQ's lemma is the edge argQ.μ1 : P[t] <- R->P[t], R[t]:pres, a
% second derivation of P beside argP.  Inside argP's term the lemma's P
% is argP's own statement, bound by the support scaffold's b: without
% primacy (argQ is not the entrypoint) it is the captured variable alone,
% the stack below argP.  Labels: P, Q IN; R[t] OUT, so the lemma is OUT.
lk.
declare P,Q,R:bool.
declare rp:(R->P).
declare pq:(P->Q).
declare qp:(Q->P).
declare nR:(~R).

argument argP : (P).
cut (Q->P) th.
axiom qp.
elim.
by default.
next.
axiom.
dixi.

argument argQ : (Q).
cut (P->Q) th.
axiom pq.
elim.
cut (R->P) th2.
axiom rp.
elim.
by default.
next.
axiom.
axiom.
dixi.

counterargument killR : (R).
cut (~R) x.
axiom nR.
elim.
axiom.
dixi.

evaluate issue :P.
evaluate argQ.
evaluate argP.
